# Supabase Authentication & RLS Implementation Plan

## Goal
Add real Supabase authentication, trip ownership (user_id), and Row Level Security to the existing GlobeTrotter app without breaking any working functionality.

## Current State
- Login/Signup pages exist but are **fake** — they use `setTimeout` to simulate auth and just `navigate('/dashboard')`
- `TripContext` uses a hardcoded `MOCK_USER` for the `user` state
- Profile page displays `MOCK_USER` data and has a "Sign out" button that just navigates to `/login`
- The `trips` table already has a `user_id UUID` column (nullable) from the original schema
- All routes are unprotected — anyone can access any page
- RLS is disabled

## Proposed Changes

---

### 1. Auth Context — `src/context/AuthContext.tsx` [NEW]

Create a dedicated authentication context that:
- Wraps the app and provides `{ user, session, loading, signIn, signUp, signOut }`
- Listens to `supabase.auth.onAuthStateChange()` for session changes
- Restores sessions on refresh via `supabase.auth.getSession()`
- `user` will be the Supabase `User` object (has `.id`, `.email`, `.user_metadata`)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is a **separate context** from `TripContext`. Auth state and trip state are independent concerns. `TripContext` will read the current user ID from `AuthContext` to filter trips.

---

### 2. Wire Login — `src/pages/Login.tsx` [MODIFY]

Replace the fake `setTimeout` login with:
```ts
const { error } = await supabase.auth.signInWithPassword({ email, password });
```
- On success: navigate to `/dashboard`
- On failure: show user-friendly error message below the form
- Keep the existing UI completely unchanged
- Wire up the email/password inputs with React state (currently uncontrolled)

---

### 3. Wire Signup — `src/pages/Signup.tsx` [MODIFY]

Replace the fake `setTimeout` signup with:
```ts
const { error } = await supabase.auth.signUp({ email, password, options: { data: { full_name: name } } });
```
- Add password match validation (confirm password field already exists)
- On success: navigate to `/dashboard`
- On failure: show error
- Keep the existing UI unchanged

---

### 4. Protected Routes — `src/App.tsx` [MODIFY]

Add a `<ProtectedRoute>` wrapper that:
- Checks `AuthContext` for an authenticated user
- If not authenticated → redirect to `/login`
- If authenticated but on `/login` or `/signup` → redirect to `/dashboard`
- Show a loading spinner while auth state is initializing

Wrap the `<AppLayout>` route group with `<ProtectedRoute>`.

---

### 5. TripContext Updates — `src/context/TripContext.tsx` [MODIFY]

Minimal changes:
- Import and use `useAuth()` to get the current user's ID
- **`fetchTrips`**: Add `.eq('user_id', userId)` filter so users only see their own trips
- **`addTrip`**: Include `user_id: userId` in the insert payload
- **`user` state**: Replace `MOCK_USER` with data derived from the Supabase auth user (id, email, display name from metadata)
- Re-fetch trips when auth user changes (dependency on userId)

---

### 6. Profile & Logout — `src/pages/Profile.tsx` [MODIFY]

- Replace `MOCK_USER` references with the real auth user data from `useAuth()`
- Wire the "Sign out" button to call `signOut()` from AuthContext (instead of `navigate('/login')`)

---

### 7. Sidebar / TopBar [NO CHANGE]

These don't reference auth directly. The Profile page handles logout. No changes needed.

---

### 8. Database Migration

**SQL to run in Supabase SQL Editor:**

```sql
-- Step 1: Enable RLS on all tables
ALTER TABLE trips ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE trip_stops ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE activities ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE expenses ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Step 2: RLS Policies for TRIPS
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own trips"
  ON trips FOR SELECT
  USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

CREATE POLICY "Users can insert own trips"
  ON trips FOR INSERT
  WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

CREATE POLICY "Users can update own trips"
  ON trips FOR UPDATE
  USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

CREATE POLICY "Users can delete own trips"
  ON trips FOR DELETE
  USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Step 3: RLS Policies for TRIP_STOPS (via trip ownership)
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own trip stops"
  ON trip_stops FOR SELECT
  USING (EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM trips WHERE trips.id = trip_stops.trip_id AND trips.user_id = auth.uid()));

CREATE POLICY "Users can insert own trip stops"
  ON trip_stops FOR INSERT
  WITH CHECK (EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM trips WHERE trips.id = trip_stops.trip_id AND trips.user_id = auth.uid()));

CREATE POLICY "Users can update own trip stops"
  ON trip_stops FOR UPDATE
  USING (EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM trips WHERE trips.id = trip_stops.trip_id AND trips.user_id = auth.uid()));

CREATE POLICY "Users can delete own trip stops"
  ON trip_stops FOR DELETE
  USING (EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM trips WHERE trips.id = trip_stops.trip_id AND trips.user_id = auth.uid()));

-- Step 4: RLS Policies for ACTIVITIES (via trip_stop → trip ownership)
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own activities"
  ON activities FOR SELECT
  USING (EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM trip_stops
    JOIN trips ON trips.id = trip_stops.trip_id
    WHERE trip_stops.id = activities.trip_stop_id AND trips.user_id = auth.uid()
  ));

CREATE POLICY "Users can insert own activities"
  ON activities FOR INSERT
  WITH CHECK (EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM trip_stops
    JOIN trips ON trips.id = trip_stops.trip_id
    WHERE trip_stops.id = activities.trip_stop_id AND trips.user_id = auth.uid()
  ));

CREATE POLICY "Users can update own activities"
  ON activities FOR UPDATE
  USING (EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM trip_stops
    JOIN trips ON trips.id = trip_stops.trip_id
    WHERE trip_stops.id = activities.trip_stop_id AND trips.user_id = auth.uid()
  ));

CREATE POLICY "Users can delete own activities"
  ON activities FOR DELETE
  USING (EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM trip_stops
    JOIN trips ON trips.id = trip_stops.trip_id
    WHERE trip_stops.id = activities.trip_stop_id AND trips.user_id = auth.uid()
  ));

-- Step 5: RLS Policies for EXPENSES (via trip ownership)
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own expenses"
  ON expenses FOR SELECT
  USING (EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM trips WHERE trips.id = expenses.trip_id AND trips.user_id = auth.uid()));

CREATE POLICY "Users can insert own expenses"
  ON expenses FOR INSERT
  WITH CHECK (EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM trips WHERE trips.id = expenses.trip_id AND trips.user_id = auth.uid()));

CREATE POLICY "Users can update own expenses"
  ON expenses FOR UPDATE
  USING (EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM trips WHERE trips.id = expenses.trip_id AND trips.user_id = auth.uid()));

CREATE POLICY "Users can delete own expenses"
  ON expenses FOR DELETE
  USING (EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM trips WHERE trips.id = expenses.trip_id AND trips.user_id = auth.uid()));
```

